sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, production containers (ADR 0263, docs/reference/production-containers.md#rollback): the rollback of a production Instance returns to old, the stopped release before live. It starts old, checks it as ready, switches the Routes and hands over the work; the rolled-away live becomes old, so a second rollback goes forward again. It selects code only. When the charts move into place, this replaces the release branch of the rollback chart.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:rollback
  %% kind: instance.rollback
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-prod Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as Old<br/>release container
  CLI->>GW: instance:rollback INSTANCE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:rollback INSTANCE`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - only the Instance: old is the one release a rollback can select
  alt the Instance has no old release
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>rollback.release_not_retained
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing changes; to go back further, deploy the earlier commit with `instance:deploy --commit`
  else old exists
    Note over GW: Admit, pause auto-deploy<br/>Instance locked · TASK
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - no started operation holds the Instance, else `operation.target_busy`
    %%> Freezes:
    %%> - live and old, the Process and Schedule definitions, the health path and the domain of each Route
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a running rollback row; automatic deploys pause and their trigger is removed
    GW->>SW: Push .env<br/>vault: env-TASK
    %%> Why:
    %%> - old gets the Instance's current `.env`, so a changed secret reaches it; secrets travel only through the vault
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>instance-rollback-production
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - no GitHub token: a rollback fetches nothing
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>TASK
    SW->>C: Write .env, start old<br/>Ansible · tags start
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes `.env` into old and starts it; its units and timers are disabled, so only FrankenPHP runs
    %%> Why no capacity check:
    %%> - no deploy runs beside a rollback, so old takes the memory that hot would take
    SW->>N: Check old is ready<br/>Ansible · tags ready
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the readiness of a deploy, without the snapshot condition: old already has its snapshot
    SW->>N: Switch the Routes<br/>Ansible · tags switch
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the same switch as a deploy: one Caddy reload; requests in progress on live finish there
    SW->>N: Hand over the work<br/>Ansible · tags handover
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - moves timers, then Processes, from live to old with the bounded graceful stop, and moves `boot.autostart`
    %%> Requirement:
    %%> - queued job payloads stay readable across one release, so old's workers can run jobs that live queued
    SW->>N: Retire, read back<br/>Ansible · tags retire · check
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - waits for native Schedule fires in the rolled-away live, then stops it; it becomes old; no container is removed
    %%> - reads back the live link, the upstream file, the commit and the Process states
    alt all steps pass
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      Note over GW: Swap live and old<br/>block rolled-away commit
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the rollback row records old's release and commit
      %%> - the rolled-away commit is blocked; automatic deploys stay paused until `instance:auto-deploy:enable`
      %%> Not included:
      %%> - no deploy step and no data change; a migration is never undone
    else a step fails before or at the switch
      SW->>C: Stop old again<br/>always · live untouched
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - live keeps serving with its work; old stays the stopped release
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error code
    else a step fails after the switch
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error code
      %%> Result:
      %%> - old serves as live; the Gateway records the release states that the run reached
    end
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
